  "question": {
    "text": "A Zener diode having break down voltage $\\mathrm{Vz}=6 \\mathrm{~V}$ is used in a voltage regulator circuit as shown in the figure. The minimum current required to pass through the Zener to act as a voltage regulator is $10 \\mathrm{~mA}$ and maximum allowed current through Zener is $40 \\mathrm{~mA}$. The maximum value of $R_{\\mathrm{s}}$ for Zener to act as a voltage regulator is\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0007_3d9188d18c8a.png\">"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$100 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$400 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$0.4 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$950 \\Omega$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0007_6d4149bf0619.png\"><br>\nMinimum current $=10 \\mathrm{~mA}\\left(\\mathrm{I}_{\\mathrm{L}}=0\\right)$\n$$\n\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{S}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{l}}=\\frac{4 \\mathrm{~V}}{10 \\mathrm{~mA}}=400 \\Omega\n$$"
  }
}